{"h":3406,"w":2400,"lines":[{"x":0.86341773047485204,"c":1,"t":"Reading","w":0.087853488922119083,"h":0.017486110828374923,"y":0.039868616317070615},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","y":0.087199060710407172,"x":0.055670099983169713,"h":0.015998613533382944,"w":0.32783505757649745,"c":1},{"w":0.88041239420572903,"x":0.055670091451352259,"h":0.01889534914976565,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.1264534882135383},{"w":0.17731959025065105,"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"y":0.14533176754874855,"x":0.053608245986283644,"t":"Passage 3 below."},{"x":0.22474228356009726,"y":0.18313953520115966,"w":0.5484535725911458,"h":0.020348836167448092,"c":1,"t":"Preface to 'How the other half thinks:"},{"w":0.58163136800130211,"h":0.024746299559973428,"t":"Adventures in mathematical reasoning'","y":0.20927051646742112,"c":1,"x":0.21023398410146057},{"w":0.8269164021809895,"c":1,"x":0.090665847335969454,"y":0.24268454239073411,"t":"Occasionally, in some difficult musical compositions, there are beautitul, but easy","h":0.020280702493502889},{"c":1,"x":0.10309277657286117,"t":"parts - parts so simple a beginner could play them. So it is with mathematics as","y":0.26159718136194376,"w":0.80206186930338552,"h":0.017615971814445075},{"c":1,"x":0.10103091540873303,"y":0.28038755142984995,"h":0.016147974163241319,"t":"well. There are some discoveries in advanced mathematics that do not depend on","w":0.82680414835611982},{"y":0.29941860437303724,"w":0.79999999999999993,"h":0.017441861012089777,"t":"specialized knowledge, not even on algebra, geometry, or trigonometry. Instead","c":1,"x":0.1010309278405352},{"w":0.82680414835611982,"y":0.31826189088288914,"c":1,"x":0.098969059735438805,"h":0.017615971814445075,"t":"they may involve, at most, a little arithmetic, such as the sum of two odd numbers"},{"y":0.33430232584796205,"t":"is even', and common sense. Each of the eight chapters in this book illustrates this","h":0.020365907105710734,"x":0.098969074804603846,"w":0.83505152384440096,"c":1},{"t":"phenomenon. Anyone can understand every step in the reasoning.","y":0.3533647457162491,"w":0.67439778645833337,"x":0.10096183803505719,"h":0.019541901136522655,"c":1},{"w":0.74432988484700524,"y":0.3837209299566422,"x":0.1010309337620643,"c":1,"t":"The thinking in each chapter uses at most only elementary arithmetic, and","h":0.017441861012089666},{"x":0.10103092410129089,"c":1,"t":"sometimes not even that. Thus all readers will have the chance to participate in a","y":0.40252495610029726,"h":0.016147974163241319,"w":0.81649485270182287},{"w":0.83711339314778643,"t":"mathematical experience, to appreciate the beauty of mathematics, and to become","x":0.098969076513677687,"y":0.42151162763104022,"h":0.017441861012089888,"c":1},{"h":0.018917539577517628,"w":0.52989690144856771,"y":0.43893129755187088,"x":0.09690722342520057,"c":1,"t":"familiar with its logical, yet intuitive, style of thinking."},{"x":0.10103093470859174,"t":"One of my purposes in writing this book is to give readers who haven't had the","h":0.01746746461950055,"w":0.78969070434570321,"y":0.46799765115503611,"c":1},{"x":0.098969067610965647,"c":1,"y":0.48678802099302354,"t":"opportunity to see and enjoy real mathematics the chance to appreciate the","w":0.76288660685221354,"h":0.017615971814445075},{"x":0.098969062100237384,"y":0.50581395321242184,"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1,"t":"mathematical way of thinking. I want to reveal not only some of the fascinating","w":0.78762888590494795},{"c":1,"w":0.63092783610026038,"x":0.098969071520845192,"y":0.52319436311980283,"t":"discoveries, but, more importantly, the reasoning behind them.","h":0.019083969465648831},{"t":"In that respect, this book differs from most books on mathematics written for the","w":0.80432322184244809,"x":0.098861032212785457,"y":0.54980524818459187,"c":1,"h":0.020642739215880002},{"c":1,"y":0.5712209303996264,"w":0.83092783610026033,"h":0.015988371754420583,"t":"general public. Some present the lives of colorful mathematicians. Others describe","x":0.098969071544121906},{"w":0.84556981404622411,"c":1,"x":0.094751131342394032,"h":0.020341249332663236,"y":0.58725402493264311,"t":"important applications of mathematics. Yet others go into mathematical procedures,"},{"t":"but assume that the reader is adept in using algebra.","x":0.098969061927411742,"h":0.017615971814445075,"y":0.60745742831045568,"w":0.53402064005533856,"c":1},{"x":0.096907208958057545,"y":0.63652378147648181,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"w":0.83298970540364592,"t":"I hope this book will help bridge that notorious gap that separates the two cultures:"},{"c":1,"y":0.65552325553802393,"w":0.81443298339843739,"h":0.017441861012089777,"t":"the humanities and the sciences, or should I say the right brain (intuitive) and the","x":0.096907219537894676},{"t":"left brain (analytical, numerical). As the chapters will illustrate, mathematics is not","h":0.017462344570014388,"y":0.67439812081734896,"c":1,"x":0.094845355211640767,"w":0.82474227905273456},{"y":0.6917204931103218,"c":1,"w":0.78556701660156236,"x":0.094845357663647767,"h":0.017615971814445186,"t":"restricted to the analytical and numerical; intuition plays a significant role. The"},{"y":0.71075581367705531,"w":0.82268040974934897,"t":"alleged gap can be narrowed or completely overcome by anyone, in part because","x":0.098969073357771914,"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.82474227905273434,"y":0.72959483245015144,"x":0.096907210879785544,"t":"each of us is far from using the full capacity of either side of the brain. To illustrate","h":0.017615971814445075},{"c":1,"h":0.017454663095793466,"t":"our human potential, I cite a structural engineer who is an artist, an electricai","y":0.74854651135157957,"w":0.7711340332031249,"x":0.098969065792070599},{"h":0.017441861012089777,"t":"engineer who is an opera singer, an opera singer who published mathematical","x":0.096907218231803635,"y":0.76744186018924021,"w":0.79175257364908869,"c":1},{"x":0.09682732905507227,"t":"research, and a mathematician who publishes short stories.","y":0.78394864571772538,"w":0.60425435384114579,"h":0.020116278513417241,"c":1},{"y":0.81385789778603457,"c":1,"t":"Other scientists have written books to explain their fields to non-scientists, but have","x":0.09896906969717463,"w":0.8391752624511718,"h":0.017615971814445186},{"x":0.096855915821188882,"h":0.019998620974618575,"t":"necessarily had to omit the mathematics, although it provides the foundation of their","y":0.82990525198651255,"c":1,"w":0.84752934773763022},{"x":0.096907223208393803,"t":"theories. The reader must remain a tantalized spectator rather than an involved","h":0.016000320963207137,"y":0.8517322370049607,"c":1,"w":0.79793813069661468},{"c":1,"x":0.096907216395898388,"t":"participant, since the appropriate language for describing the details in much of","y":0.87052260718773167,"w":0.80000000000000004,"h":0.016147974163241319},{"t":"science is mathematics, whether the subject is expanding universe, subatomic","h":0.017441861012089777,"x":0.096907218228122746,"w":0.79175257364908858,"y":0.88953488344507381,"c":1},{"w":0.81649485270182287,"y":0.90692894875263808,"x":0.096907212754491073,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"t":"particles, or chromosomes. Though the broad outline of a scientific theory can be"},{"c":1,"h":0.022583511809496359,"t":"leltsresources.org","y":0.95433624955947682,"x":0.35219444028158703,"w":0.29146217346191411},{"y":0.94912790685216741,"w":0.026804122924804719,"t":"73","h":0.013081395479068947,"x":0.91546391781594816,"c":1}]}